assessed(106,2006,[15,13,12,9,8,7,4,4,2,1.5],-10,0,null,'comparative cost-benefit analysis of global interventions','The book explains ranked tradeoffs and competing proposals rather than a procedural spending manual. Policy advocacy does not establish ideological capture.', 'Expert papers and counterarguments support estimates with uncertain valuations|Connects health, trade, governance, resources and development|Explicit opportunity costs transfer across allocation decisions|Explains intervention pathways and cost-benefit assumptions|Concise paired challenges and priorities concentrate analytical content|Allocation logic persists while numerical estimates date|Quantification and resource management fit despite unwanted applied themes|Contributors have relevant economics and policy expertise|A common budget question organizes diverse interventions|Quantified comparisons are clear but depend on value assumptions', ['https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/abs/how-to-spend-50-billion-to-make-the-world-a-better-place/introduction/C62CECC82D3EEDBEF8BFF4B6E61AD2E3','https://assets.cambridge.org/97805218/66798/frontmatter/9780521866798_frontmatter.pdf'],{author:'Bjørn Lomborg, editor',themeNote:'T11 -10: disease, hunger and environmental interventions dominate the ranked global problems. T12 0: comparative resource management is the organizing question, not finance or political power.',yearConfidence:'high'});
assessed(107,2020,[17,9,9,8,8,8,2,5,2.5,1.5],-10,0,null,'psychological explanation of language and social judgment','Experimental social-cognition research supplies transferable models of signaling and bias. Inclusion advocacy alone is not a veto.', 'Research and experiments substantiate language-based judgment with scope limits|Connects childhood learning, identity, perception and economic opportunity|Signaling and judgment-bias lessons transfer to organizations|Explains how learned speech cues influence affiliation and evaluation|Focused examples and research support a concentrated argument|Language-based social categorization remains durable|Cognition and institutions fit indirectly, with little technical application|Kinzler conducts relevant developmental and social-psychology research|A central overlooked cue gives the book a clear narrative|Clear distinctions connect experimental findings to everyday examples', ['https://dsclab.uchicago.edu/howyousayit/','https://news.uchicago.edu/profile/katherine-d-kinzler','https://www.everand.com/book/726410393/How-You-Say-It-Why-We-Judge-Others-by-the-Way-They-Talk-and-the-Costs-of-This-Hidden-Bias'],{themeNote:'T11 -10: identity, discrimination and minority-related social judgment are central. T12 0: cognitive mechanisms, not political power.',yearNote:'Original copyright and publication 2020 are reproduced in the cited primary front matter; paperback subtitle and 2021 issue do not reset it.'});
assessed(108,1991,[16,10,9,7,8,8,2,5,2,1.5],0,0,null,'anthropological argument about human universals','A sustained comparative argument with historical and illustrative exposition passes the expert exception. The hypothetical Universal People is an explanatory device, not a fictional main work.', 'Cross-cultural cases support universals, with sampling and absence-of-exception limits|Connects culture, behavior, language and human psychology|Distinguishing universal constraints from local variation aids model building|Catalogs patterns more strongly than it identifies their causes|A compact comparative argument contains substantial distinctions|Human commonalities remain useful despite later refinements|Indirect relevance through modeling and cultural constraints|Brown has specialist anthropological research experience|History, examples and a synthetic portrait organize the argument|Careful universality distinctions matter, though evidence can be uneven', ['https://books.google.com/books/about/Human_Universals.html?hl=en&id=YQPFQgAACAAJ&output=html_text','https://literary-universals.uconn.edu/2017/06/25/human-universals/'],{themeNote:'T11 0: comparative anthropology rather than a particular minority or national history. T12 0: empirical human-pattern analysis rather than philosophy or political power.',eligibilityConfidence:'moderate'});
assessed(109,2013,[12,3,4,2,4,6,0,2,2.5,1.5],-10,0,null,'illustrated autobiographical humor','V3: personal comic episodes and depictions of depression yield recognition but little explicit causal or strategic model after their particular situations are removed.', 'First-person scenes convey experience rather than general psychological evidence|Family, pets and inner experience supply little systems integration|Some emotional recognition survives, but explicit reusable models are scarce|Depicts feelings and events rather than explaining causal systems|Visual humor dominates over analytical information density|Personal experiences retain literary value but limited durable analysis|No substantial direct technical or industrial fit|Brosh has experiential and artistic authority rather than research standing|Text-image sequencing gives episodes effective comic structure|Exaggeration serves expression rather than conceptual precision', ['https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Hyperbole-and-a-Half/Allie-Brosh/9781451666182'],{veto:['V3'],vetoConfidence:'moderate',themeNote:'T11 -10: depression and personal illness experience are a central substantial strand. T12 0: autobiographical humor is not primarily philosophical or political.'});
assessed(110,2018,[14,11,9,7,8,7,2,4,2.5,1.5],-10,-10,null,'argument about recognition and identity politics','Recognition offers a reusable model, with broad explanatory ambition limiting causal confidence. Reform proposals and political positions do not establish V5.', 'Historical and contemporary examples support a selective synthetic argument|Connects psychology, institutions, nationalism and political movements|Recognition and legitimacy offer transferable interpretive models|A unifying motive explains patterns but underweights alternative causes|A short focused thesis keeps the treatment relatively dense|Recognition problems persist beyond the current populist cycle|Institutional power fits indirectly; technical systems are absent|Fukuyama has sustained political-development scholarship|Conceptual origins and modern cases form a clear progression|Readable argument sometimes compresses different forms of identity', ['https://us.macmillan.com/books/9780374717483/identity/','https://fukuyama.people.stanford.edu/identity'],{themeNote:'T11 -10: identity and minority-related political issues dominate. T12 -10: politics and philosophical recognition.'});
assessed(111,2003,[15,12,12,8,7,8,3,5,2.5,1.5],-10,-10,2002,'memoir of financial and public-policy decisions under uncertainty','Explicit probabilistic decision principles survive the personal narrative. Retrospective executive self-selection lowers evidence without eliminating the payload.', 'Direct decision access is rich, with selective retrospective justification|Connects markets, international crises, fiscal policy and institutions|Probabilistic thinking and risk tradeoffs transfer broadly|Explains decision constraints more than isolating all macroeconomic causes|Substantial episodes support principles with some personal detail|Decision discipline remains durable beyond individual crises|Quantitative strategic thinking fits indirectly through finance|Rubin had direct market and Treasury decision authority|Business and government episodes reinforce a common decision theme|Uncertainty is expressed more carefully than in many executive memoirs', ['https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/158625/in-an-uncertain-world-by-robert-e-rubin-and-jacob-weisberg/'],{author:'Robert E. Rubin and Jacob Weisberg',themeNote:'T11 -10: American political-figure and institutional memoir. T12 -10: finance and politics.',periodNote:'The narrative reaches the post-September-11 economy before 2003 publication; 2002 is a moderate-confidence endpoint.',yearConfidence:'high'});
assessed(112,2006,[13,9,7,6,6,8,2,3,2.5,1.5],-10,-10,1800,'history of the early American press','Partisan incentives and information control provide transferable lessons. Narrative emphasis and source limitations reduce the score rather than justify V3.', 'Historical reporting is informative but less rigorous than specialist source scholarship|Connects printing, political factions, personalities and public opinion|Partisan media incentives transfer across communication environments|Explains press-politics interaction more than broader causal identification|Colorful episodes and repeated excesses reduce density|Media incentives and factional conflict remain durable|Institutional power fits indirectly, technical printing detail is secondary|Burns has journalism expertise rather than deep early-American archival specialization|Personalities sustain an accessible historical narrative|Vivid prose sometimes overstates the era’s uniform partisanship', ['https://www.hachettebookgroup.com/titles/eric-burns/infamous-scribblers/9781586485436/','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infamous_Scribblers'],{themeNote:'T11 -10: American national history and political figures. T12 -10: media and politics.',periodConfidence:'moderate',periodNote:'Central founding-era press narrative is assessed through the early republic around 1800.',yearNote:'Original 2006 edition is identified in the bibliographic history; the publisher page is the 2007 edition. Moderate confidence.'});
assessed(114,2012,[13,10,11,8,7,7,3,3,2,1.5],0,-10,null,'argument about corporate language and governance','Comparative CEO communications support a general governance argument, beyond a narrow trading procedure. Predictive-performance claims receive restrained evidence credit.', 'Comparative statements support candor patterns, while prediction claims need independent validation|Connects language, incentives, governance and business performance|Attention to specificity and accountability transfers across organizations|Explains signaling and information concealment more than proving returns|Case comparisons are useful but some claims repeat|Communication discipline is durable even as company examples age|Institutional quality fits indirectly through finance|Rittenhouse has relevant financial-analysis and corporate-communication practice|A common candor framework organizes company comparisons|The emphasis on precise commitments is useful, though branded measures need care', ['https://www.mheducation.com/highered/mhp/product/investing-between-lines-pb.html'],{themeNote:'T11 0: company comparisons have broad application. T12 -10: investor decisions and corporate finance are central.',yearNote:'Publisher lists copyright 2012; 2023 paperback publication is a reprint. Original production year 2012 retained.',eligibilityConfidence:'moderate'});
assessed(90,2011,[15,10,11,8,8,8,3,4,2.5,1.5],0,0,null,'argument about philanthropic strategy and accountability','Six strategic questions and institutional examples explain effective giving beyond a procedural donation manual. Resource-allocation lessons transfer.', 'Foundation experience and cases support conclusions with limited causal testing|Connects goals, resources, institutions and measurement|Goal clarity and evaluation transfer across resource-allocation decisions|Explains incentives and feedback behind ineffective giving|A small question set keeps the argument focused|Accountability and allocation problems remain durable|Resource management and institutional quality fit indirectly|Authors have relevant philanthropy research and advising experience|Questions and examples provide a clear cumulative structure|Terms and practical distinctions are generally clear', ['https://www.hachettebookgroup.com/titles/thomas-j-tierney/give-smart/9781586489892/'],{author:'Thomas J. Tierney and Joel L. Fleishman',themeNote:'T11 0: strategy has general application beyond American examples. T12 0: philanthropic resource allocation, not finance as an end, is central.'});
assessed(92,1994,[18,13,10,11,9,8,5,5,2,2],-10,0,null,'explanatory account of climate science and policy choices','The primary preface addresses general readers and gives a sustained science-to-policy account. Classroom use does not alone override that explanatory purpose; no explicit exam or technical-reference intent controls.', 'Scientific assessments ground the account and distinguish sources of uncertainty|Connects radiation, climate, impacts, economics, energy and policy|Uncertainty and physical-constraint reasoning transfer across systems|Explains causal physical mechanisms with accessible quantitative detail|Compact chapters and diagrams carry substantial explanatory content|Physical principles endure though numerical projections and policy context age|Physics and energy fit, but familiar basics and ecology reduce novelty|Houghton has direct climate-science and assessment authority|A cumulative science-to-response structure aids understanding|Scientific quantities and qualification are treated carefully', ['https://assets.cambridge.org/97805217/09163/frontmatter/9780521709163_frontmatter.pdf','https://assets.cambridge.org/97805215/28740/frontmatter/9780521528740_frontmatter.pdf'],{eligibilityConfidence:'moderate',yearConfidence:'high',yearNote:'Cambridge copyright page explicitly states first published 1994 by Lion Publishing; subsequent editions do not reset original production age.',themeNote:'T11 -10: climate and environmental effects are central. T12 0: physical science is the central framework, with policy auxiliary.'});
assessed(96,2020,[13,13,11,8,7,7,4,4,2.5,1.5],0,-10,null,'comparison of US and Chinese strategic strengths','A civilizational inclination and geopolitical proposals are not enough for V2 or V5. Selected comparisons reduce evidence confidence while strategic constraints remain useful.', 'Comparative observations are informative but some favorable framing is selective|Connects economics, institutions, strategy, culture and international order|Perspective-taking and strategic restraint transfer beyond the bilateral case|Explains incentives and constraints more than testing national causal claims|A focused argument repeats some policy themes|Structural rivalry outlasts individual administrations|Geostrategy and institutional power fit; technology is secondary|Mahbubani has relevant diplomatic and policy experience|Contrasting strategic choices give a readable structure|Clear prose sometimes turns broad national tendencies into generalizations', ['https://www.hachettebookgroup.com/titles/kishore-mahbubani/has-china-won/9781541706569/','https://books.google.com/books?id=sDyezQEACAAJ'],{themeNote:'T11 0: bilateral rivalry with global influence, not single-nation history. T12 -10: geopolitics.',yearNote:'Original publication 2020 is established by the cited bibliographic record; 2026 publisher edition is later.'});
assessed(97,2009,[15,12,10,9,8,7,3,4,2,1.5],-10,-10,null,'argument about coordinated healthcare reform','The title’s user-guide wording does not make the book a procedural treatment manual: the content explains incentives, coordination and system redesign.', 'Practitioner evidence grounds a policy argument with organizational interests|Connects payment, care coordination, quality and institutions|Feedback and service-integration lessons transfer across complex organizations|Explains fragmentation and incentives that obstruct system improvement|A short system-level argument concentrates on the main constraints|Coordination problems endure while specific reforms change|Quality and resource management fit indirectly|Halvorson has relevant health-system executive experience|Problem diagnosis and redesign form a coherent progression|Clear organizational language keeps the main mechanisms explicit', ['https://www.routledge.com/Health-Care-Will-Not-Reform-Itself-A-Users-Guide-to-Refocusing-and-Reforming/Halvorson/p/book/9781439816141'],{themeNote:'T11 -10: American healthcare. T12 -10: reform policy and financing are central.',eligibilityConfidence:'moderate'});
